exercises.prompt:
Read:

def is_even(n):
    return n % 2 == 0

if is_even(8):
    print("even")

What prints?

You can combine two checks with and:

def is_even(n):
    return n % 2 == 0

def is_positive(n):
    return n > 0

if is_even(6) and is_positive(6):
    print("both")

What prints?

Predict:

if is_even(6) and is_positive(-6):
    print("both")
else:
    print("not both")

Combine the two checks so BOTH must hold:

if is_even(n) ____ is_positive(n):
    print("ok")

Build a bigger check from a small one:

def is_even(n):
    return n % 2 == 0

def is_odd(n):
    return not is_even(n)

print(is_odd(7))

Predict:

def is_even(n):
    return n % 2 == 0

def is_odd(n):
    return not is_even(n)

print(is_odd(10))
